CAT = "pjpolPoliceOrder"; SEG = "POL"
# Policing in Punjab and the Police Order 2002 (articles as in the 2002 text).
Q = [
("The Police Order 2002 replaced which earlier law?",
 "The Police Act 1861", ["The Penal Code 1860", "The Police Rules 1934", "The Evidence Act 1872"],
 "Article 185 of the Police Order 2002 repealed the Police Act 1861, the colonial law that had governed the police for over 140 years."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, the head of police of a province, of the rank of Inspector General, is called the:",
 "Provincial Police Officer", ["Regional Police Officer", "Chief Police Commissioner", "District Police Officer"],
 "The Order calls the IG who heads a province's police the Provincial Police Officer (PPO)."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, who heads the police of an ordinary district?",
 "District Police Officer", ["Station House Officer", "Deputy Commissioner", "Regional Police Officer"],
 "Article 16 vests the administration of police in a district in the District Police Officer (DPO). The Deputy Commissioner heads the civil administration."),
("The head of police of Lahore, Punjab's capital city district, is called the:",
 "Capital City Police Officer", ["City Police Officer", "District Police Officer", "Additional Inspector General"],
 "The Order names the head of police of a capital city district the Capital City Police Officer (CCPO), and Punjab Police calls the head of Lahore police the CCPO Lahore."),
("Which of these is a duty of every police officer under Article 4 of the Police Order 2002?",
 "Take charge of unclaimed property", ["Decide bail in serious cases", "Sentence petty offenders on the spot", "Collect income tax"],
 "Article 4 includes taking charge of all unclaimed property and preparing its inventory. Bail and sentencing are for courts."),
("Article 3 of the Police Order 2002 tells every officer to treat members of the public with:",
 "Due decorum and courtesy", ["Strict suspicion", "Distance and silence", "Firm military discipline"],
 "Article 3 begins with the duty to behave with members of the public with due decorum and courtesy and to promote amity."),
("Under Article 4, when a person is arrested, the police must promptly tell:",
 "A person of his choice", ["The Union Council chairman", "His employer", "The newspapers"],
 "Article 4 makes it a duty to ensure that information about an arrest is promptly communicated to a person of the arrested person's choice."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, an officer who is off duty or on leave:",
 "Can still be called for duty", ["Cannot be called back", "Loses all his police powers", "Must hand in his card"],
 "Article 115 says a police officer off duty, on leave or under suspension is liable to be called for duty."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, may a serving police officer take up private employment?",
 "No, it is not allowed", ["Yes, after duty hours", "Yes, with a DSP's approval", "Only in his home district"],
 "Article 117 bars any police officer from engaging in private employment while a member of the police establishment."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, who is the appointing authority for constables and other junior ranks?",
 "Head of District Police", ["Provincial Police Officer", "Chief Secretary", "Public Service Commission"],
 "Article 23 makes the Head of District Police the appointing authority for junior ranks."),
("On appointment, under the Police Order 2002 every member of the police must:",
 "Make an oath or affirmation", ["Deposit a security bond", "Pass a driving test", "Serve a year without any pay"],
 "Article 24 requires every member of the police to make and subscribe an oath or affirmation on appointment."),
("A junior-rank officer's certificate of appointment becomes void when he:",
 "Ceases to belong to the police", ["Goes on annual leave", "Is promoted to Head Constable", "Is posted to another district police"],
 "Article 25 says the certificate of appointment becomes null and void whenever the officer ceases to belong to the police."),
("Under Article 125, a police officer who on reasonable grounds suspects a vehicle in a street of carrying unlawful goods may:",
 "Search it", ["Confiscate it permanently", "Fine the owner on the spot", "Auction its contents"],
 "Article 125 lets an officer search a suspected person or vehicle and, if the account given is suspicious, detain the article with a written receipt."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, being found intoxicated while on duty is:",
 "Punishable misconduct", ["A matter of leave only", "Allowed off the station", "A minor warning only"],
 "Article 155 makes being found in a state of intoxication on duty an offence punishable with imprisonment and fine."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, an officer who inflicts torture on a person in custody:",
 "Commits a punishable offence", ["Acts within his powers", "Faces only a transfer", "Needs a DSP's sanction first"],
 "Article 156 makes torture or violence to a person in custody punishable with imprisonment of up to five years and fine."),
("Which register at a police station must record complainants, persons arrested and property taken?",
 "Daily Diary", ["Case Property Book", "Duty Roster", "Visitors' Book"],
 "Article 167 requires a register of Daily Diary at every police station recording complainants, arrests, offences, property and witnesses."),
("Citizen Police Liaison Committees under the Police Order 2002 are:",
 "Voluntary, self-financing bodies", ["Units of the Pakistan Army", "Courts for minor cases", "Wings of the Special Branch"],
 "Article 168 lets the Government set up CPLCs as voluntary, self-financing and autonomous bodies to link aggrieved citizens with the police."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, unclaimed property found by a police officer must be:",
 "Listed in an inventory", ["Given to the finder", "Sold within a week", "Kept by the officer himself"],
 "Article 134 makes it every officer's duty to take charge of unclaimed property, make an inventory and send a copy to the Head of District Police."),
("The Punjab Police Code of Conduct says an officer offered a bribe must:",
 "Report it to his senior at once", ["Return it the next day", "Accept it as evidence", "Ignore it and say nothing about it"],
 "The Code requires every officer offered a bribe to make an immediate report to his senior; failing to do so is a breach of discipline."),
("The Punjab Police Code of Conduct says force used against an individual must be:",
 "The minimum necessary", ["Enough to deter others", "Decided by the crowd", "Equal to the offence"],
 "The Code says an officer defending himself or enforcing his authority shall use minimum force, and never more than is reasonable."),
("Before a crowd is declared an unlawful assembly and ordered to disperse, the Code of Conduct says police should first try:",
 "Warnings and persuasion", ["Firing in the air", "Arresting the leaders", "Cutting the electricity"],
 "The Code says all attempts to disperse a crowd by warnings and exhortations must be made before it is declared unlawful."),
("Which of these is the correct order of ranks, lowest first?",
 "Constable, Head Constable, ASI", ["Head Constable, Constable, ASI", "ASI, Head Constable, Constable", "Constable, ASI, Head Constable"],
 "The junior ranks run Constable, Head Constable, Assistant Sub-Inspector, then Sub-Inspector and Inspector."),
("The officer in charge of a police station is commonly called the:",
 "Station House Officer", ["Sub-Divisional Police Officer", "District Police Officer", "Reserve Inspector"],
 "The Station House Officer (SHO) runs a police station. A Sub-Divisional Police Officer (SDPO), usually a DSP, supervises the police stations of a circle."),
("A police region in Punjab, made up of several districts, is headed by the:",
 "Regional Police Officer", ["District Police Officer", "Station House Officer", "Divisional Commissioner"],
 "A Regional Police Officer (RPO), an officer of Deputy Inspector General rank or above, supervises the districts of a region, such as Sargodha or Bahawalpur."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, direct recruitment into the police (other than ministerial and specialist cadres) is made in the ranks of Constable, ASI and:",
 "Assistant Superintendent", ["Inspector", "Head Constable", "Deputy Superintendent of Police"],
 "Article 7(3) provides for recruitment at three entry points: Constable, Assistant Sub-Inspector and Assistant Superintendent of Police."),
("Where is the headquarters of the Punjab Police?",
 "Central Police Office, Lahore", ["Police Lines, Rawalpindi", "Civil Secretariat, South Punjab", "Police House, Faisalabad"],
 "The Inspector General of Police, Punjab works from the Central Police Office in Lahore, which also issues the constable recruitment advertisements."),
("Under the Police Order 2002, wearing police uniform without authority by someone who is not a police officer is:",
 "A punishable offence", ["Allowed at weddings", "Allowed for retired staff", "Only a civil wrong"],
 "Article 151 makes unauthorised wearing of police uniform, or a dress resembling it, an offence punishable on conviction."),
("Under Article 157, a police officer who vexatiously delays sending an arrested person to court:",
 "Can be punished", ["Earns a commendation", "Must pay the accused's fare", "Loses one day's leave only"],
 "Article 157 makes unnecessary delay in forwarding an arrested person to a court an offence punishable with imprisonment and fine."),
]
